## Why This Question Is Asked
Tests the ability to design per-tenant traffic control across data centers, implement dynamic configuration updates, and establish observability—all without service downtime.

## Key Concepts
- **Deterministic hashing**: Ensures consistent per-tenant canary decisions across all service instances
- **Docker Config**: Enables dynamic configuration reloads and zero-downtime rollouts
- **Multi-DC routing**: Traefik handles TLS termination with per-tenant observability across both data centers

## Code Example
```javascript
function isCanary(tenant, percentage) {
  const hash = [...tenant].reduce((acc, char) => (acc * 31 + char.charCodeAt(0)) >>> 0, 0);
  return (hash % 100) < percentage;
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests edge routing with simple feature flag logic using standard nginx capabilities, keeping it beginner-friendly while still requiring practical setup.

## Key Concepts
- nginx upstreams and map for header-driven routing
- TLS termination in docker-compose
- cross-DC networking and service naming

## Code Example
```nginx
http {
  upstream api-old { server api-old:8080; }
  upstream api-new { server api-new:8080; }
  map $http_x_feature_flag_alpha $target { default api-old; 1 api-new; }
  server {
    listen 443 ssl;
    ssl_certificate /certs/server.crt; ssl_certificate_key /certs/server.key;
    location / { proxy_pass http://$target; }
  }
}
```

